\section*{AP \({ }^{\text {® }}\) CALCULUS BC \\ 2007 SCORING GUIDELINES}

\section*{Question 2}

The amount of water in a storage tank, in gallons, is modeled by a continuous function on the time interval \(0 \leq t \leq 7\), where \(t\) is measured in hours. In this model, rates are given as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] The rate at which water enters the tank is \(f(t)=100 t^{2} \sin (\sqrt{t})\) gallons per hour for \(0 \leq t \leq 7\).
\item[(ii)] The rate at which water leaves the tank is \(g(t)=\left\{\begin{array}{r}250 \text { for } 0 \leq t<3 \\ 2000 \text { for } 3<t \leq 7\end{array}\right.\) gallons per hour.
\end{itemize}
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/4ff36bbc-0e5c-4a7e-aa8f-a00d82d03863-1.jpg?height=455&width=662&top_left_y=378&top_left_x=1220)
The graphs of \(f\) and \(g\), which intersect at \(t=1.617\) and \(t=5.076\), are shown in the figure above. At time \(t=0\), the amount of water in the tank is 5000 gallons.
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] How many gallons of water enter the tank during the time interval \(0 \leq t \leq 7\) ? Round your answer to the nearest gallon.
\item[(b)] For \(0 \leq t \leq 7\), find the time intervals during which the amount of water in the tank is decreasing. Give a reason for each answer.
\item[(c)] For \(0 \leq t \leq 7\), at what time \(t\) is the amount of water in the tank greatest? To the nearest gallon, compute the amount of water at this time. Justify your answer.
\item[(a)] \(\int_{0}^{7} f(t) d t \approx 8264\) gallons
\item[(b)] The amount of water in the tank is decreasing on the intervals \(0 \leq t \leq 1.617\) and \(3 \leq t \leq 5.076\) because \(f(t)<g(t)\) for \(0 \leq t<1.617\) and \(3<t<5.076\).
\item[(c)] Since \(f(t)-g(t)\) changes sign from positive to negative only at \(t=3\), the candidates for the absolute maximum are at \(t=0,3\), and 7 .

\begin{tabular}[t]{|l|l|}
\hline \(t\) (hours) & gallons of water \\
\hline 0 & 5000 \\
\hline 3 & \(5000+\int_{0}^{3} f(t) d t-250(3)=5126.591\) \\
\hline 7 & \(5126.591+\int_{3}^{7} f(t) d t-2000(4)=4513.807\) \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
The amount of water in the tank is greatest at 3 hours. At that time, the amount of water in the tank, rounded to the nearest gallon, is 5127 gallons.
\end{itemize}
